<!-- 
question - how can we genarate report using Extentreportmanager

Answer - To generate report using ExtentReportManager , we make use of ITestListner Interface provided by testNg .
		- we create a separate class (for Example - EXtentReportmanager.java) and implements the ITestListner Interface .
		
		- ITestListner provided several callback methods such as 
		1- onStart() - called before the testExecution begins.
		2-onFinish() - called after all test have finished .
		3- onTestSuccess() -  triggered when a test case passes.
		4- onTestFailure()- triggered when a test case failed .
		5- onTestSkipped() - triggered when a test is skipped .
		
		
 -->